Nook

Nook is a fork of Coucou by Louis Raillé (https://github.com/Louis-CFM/coucou),
built on the Windows multi-session work by Edurique
(https://github.com/Edurique/coucou_edu_windows_implementation).

The code is MIT-licensed; see LICENSE, which keeps the original copyright notice.
Coucou's own name, character, icons and sounds are not part of Nook: Nook's
character, icons and sounds are its own; see LICENSE-ASSETS.md.

Nook is not affiliated with or endorsed by Coucou's author.

Icons
-----

The interface icons are from Lucide (https://lucide.dev), and the GitHub and X
marks in the settings window's About section, and the Cursor mark that labels its sessions, are from Simple Icons
(https://simpleicons.org). Only the icons used are in the code, as the shapes
of their SVG files (windows/src/views/iconset.ts).

